# ==========================================================================
# Keeps secrets and local data OUT of the image.
#
# backend/Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so without this file every one of
# these would be baked into a layer that anyone with the image can extract:
#   - .env                -> live CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY / AI_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   - social_media.db     -> encrypted credentials and all your content
#   - .venv/              -> hundreds of MB of local dependencies
#   - media/              -> every uploaded file
#
# Excluded files are still fully present in your local checkout and in git.
# ==========================================================================

# ---- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ---- local data ------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
media/

# ---- virtualenvs and caches ------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# ---- not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------
tests/
pytest.ini
*.md

# ---- tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------
.dockerignore
.git/
.gitignore